A Network architectures
The detailed architecture of the proposed adaptive module on top of FPN is shown in Fig. 5. Adaptive modules are applied on top of the standard Feature Pyramid Network (FPN) [26]. For each view image with an input shape of H × W × 3, the backbone and FPN output multi-scale features F2, F3, F4, F5 with shapes of H/4×W/4×C, H/8×W/8×C, H/16×W/16×C, H/32×W/32×C. The adaptive module upsamples the multi-scale features into shape H/4 × W/4 × C via “torch.nn.Upsample”, “torch.nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d” operations, and a 1 × 1 convolution layer. Then, the sampled features are concatenated together followed by a 1 × 1 convolution layer to get this view image feature with a shape of H/4 × W/4 × C. Our model can benefit from the FPN concatenation mechanisms in recent works such as [16, 54].
